.nh
.TH "SOROLENS" "1" "Nov 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
sorolens-inspect - Show detailed information about a tracked contract or a transaction


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsorolens inspect  | inspect --tx  [contract-id] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show detailed information about a tracked contract, or with --tx about a
single transaction: its function, status, resource usage and emitted events.

.PP
With --tx the contract is looked up from the transaction hash. Pass a contract
ID as well to skip that lookup.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for inspect

.PP
\fB--tx\fP=""
	Inspect a transaction by its hash instead of a contract


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API key for authenticating with the Sorolens API

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Sorolens API base URL

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--network\fP=""
	Stellar network (testnet, mainnet, futurenet, standalone)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--output\fP=""
	Output format (table, json, yaml or jsonl)

.PP
\fB--plugin-api-key\fP[=false]
	When dispatching to a plugin, pass the active profile's API key as SOROLENS_API_KEY (off by default)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Configuration profile name (default: $SOROLENS_PROFILE, then the default profile)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	jq-style path filter applied to structured output (e.g. '.items[].name')

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=10s
	Request timeout


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  sorolens inspect CAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA
  sorolens inspect --tx <64-hex-hash>
  sorolens inspect --tx <64-hex-hash> <contract-id> --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsorolens(1)\fP
